<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MuckrakerChassis_TheftHauler.xml     TheftHauler · BUILDING_THEFT_HAULER_1

  The ONE wiring point between the generic engine (this mod) and the reused
  Droidworks chassis (item spec: "reuse an existing Droidworks heavy chassis
  ... do not invent a new race"). RSW_DW_Race_OuterRim_MuckrakerDroid (the
  "Muckraker Crab Droid") is the largest-bodied concrete Droidworks race
  measured across every Races_*.xml file (baseBodySize 1.2 — every other
  concrete droid tops out at 1.0), and its DW_Family_Labour ancestry is a
  work chassis, not a combat one — the closest existing fit to a "heavy
  hauler" without inventing new art.

  Adds RimMandrake.TheftHauler.TheftHaulerExtension as a NEW modExtensions
  node directly on the concrete def. AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace inherits
  DW_Family_Labour's own modExtensions (DroidworksExtension) via standard
  RimWorld list-inheritance APPEND (no Inherit="False" here or on the
  parent) — this patch's own li joins that list rather than replacing it,
  so DroidworksExtension's power/energy tuning survives untouched.

  MayRequire-gated: absent Droidworks, this file is a silent no-op and the
  engine mod (JobDef/JobDriver/FloatMenuOptionProvider/marker class) stays
  fully functional for any OTHER pawnkind a player or another content mod
  marks directly with the extension.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">
    <mods>
      <li>Droidworks</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/AlienRace.ThingDef_AlienRace[defName="RSW_DW_Race_OuterRim_MuckrakerDroid"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <modExtensions>
          <li Class="RimMandrake.TheftHauler.TheftHaulerExtension" />
        </modExtensions>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
